The U.S. state of [[Minnesota]] first required its residents to register their [[motor vehicle]]s in 1903. Registrants provided their own [[Vehicle registration plate|license plate]]s for display until 1909, when the state began to issue plates.

{{As of|2024}}, plates are issued by the [[Minnesota Department of Public Safety]] through its Driver and Vehicle Services Division. Front and rear plates are required for most classes of vehicles, while only rear plates are required for motorcycles and trailers.

==Passenger baseplates==
[[File:First Minnesota license plate.jpg|thumb|left|The first automobile license plate in Minnesota, 1903.]]
